// Golden vectors, determinism, resume, the stage entry point, the schema
// and the pipeline of the regions stage (spec P1-06 sections 2, 3, 5 RG14,
// 6 invariant 7, 10.1 tests 5 and 6, 10.3 and 10.4; P0-02 amendment 17;
// P1-00 sections 3, 10.1 and 14 X1, X2; D10).
//
// The golden vectors in worldgen/tests/golden/p1-06-regions.txt were
// generated by worldgen/tests/reference/p1_regions_reference.py, the test
// writer's exact-integer reference written from the spec alone, on input
// layers checked against p1-05-resources.txt. Each case's thirteen inputs
// are recomputed by the earlier stages and compared first, so an upstream
// change shows as such. The items are then compared in step order, so a
// failure names the first step that diverges: drainage height (the shared
// G7 seam), the cost noise and weight (seams region_cost_noise,
// region_step_weight), the candidates and seeds (region_candidates,
// region_seeds, region_landmass_seeds), the flood (region_flood), the merge
// (region_merge), and the layer and the three tables (regions_stage), each
// also against the test's own steps (p1_06_regions_support.hpp).
//
// The N >= 512 cases run in the suite "regions-slow":
//   worldgen-tests -ts=regions-slow --no-skip

